-- Title: Dynamic Strings Library
-- Author: Matthew Schinkel
-- Compiler: 3.0a1
--
-- This file is part of jallib (https://github.com/jallib/jallib)
-- Released under the BSD license (http://www.opensource.org/licenses/bsd-license.php)
--
-- Description: Helper API for heap-backed dynamic strings.
--
-- Notes:
-- - Heap byte count is **`const word _string_heap_size = N`** (compile-time constant).
--   **`pragma string heap N`** is accepted for compatibility and **ignored** (no diagnostic).
--   Put it **before** other **`pragma string …`** lines that depend on heap size
--   (e.g. **`pragma string index auto`**) and **before** **`include strings_dynamic`**
--   / the first dynamic **`var string`** (see **`docs/language.md`**).
-- - `include strings_dynamic` pulls in JAL **`string_*`** wrappers; **`_string_*`**
--   builtins are recognized by the compiler whenever spelled (**`jal_string_builtin_is`**
--   in **`src/jal/jal_string.c`**).
-- - **Canonical builtin token**: **`_string_*`** (one underscore before the public
--   name). **`string_*`** here are normal JAL **`function`** entries.
-- - **`string_append`**, **`string_heap_compact`**, and the other **`string_*`**
--   wrappers are **not** **`pragma inline`**: each JAL **`call`** hits one shared
--   forwarder body that delegates to **`_string_*`** builtins (PIC18 ROM **B/C**).
--   **`string_heap_compact()`** is still parsed as a **compiler builtin** (deferred
--   pcode expand), so Phase-B compact logic is **not** a separate machine **`call`**
--   block in **`-asm`** the way a normal outlined JAL procedure is — see
-- § Broader ROM plan.
--   **`string_from_array`**, **`string_from_array_truncate`**,
--   **`string_to_array`**, and **`string_to_array_truncate`** are the same pattern;
--   the compiler accepts open-array formals for the byte-array
--   operand of these builtins.
--
-- Compiler-backed helper signatures (wrappers below):
--
-- function string_append(string in out dst, string in src) return bit
-- function string_append_truncate(string in out dst, string in src, word in max_len) return bit
-- function string_truncate(string in out dst, word in max_len) return bit
-- function string_from_array(string in out dst, byte in src_array[]) return bit
-- function string_from_array_truncate(string in out dst, byte in src_array[], word in max_len) return bit
-- function string_to_array(byte out dst_array[], string in src) return bit
-- function string_to_array_truncate(byte out dst_array[], string in src, word in max_len) return bit
-- function string_heap_compact() return bit
--
-- Truncating helpers return FALSE when bytes are dropped. They do not set
-- _string_error merely because truncation occurred.
-- string_heap_compact() (Phase B): pack the string heap, patch all dynamic
--    handles, rebuild the free list; supports pragma string index byte|word.
--    Fails (FALSE) if the work table would exceed the compiler’s array-size
--    limit (see fix_string_heap_compact_work_table_rows.md) or the heap
--    runtime is missing. On PIC18, the work buffer is one GPR array of
--    4×(dynamic-string count)×(index width) bytes; with pragma string index
--    word and many handles it may not fit a single 256-byte bank (byte index
--    keeps rows 4 bytes each for the same handle count).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Description: Append dynamic string src to dst (delegates to builtin).
-- Parameters:
-- - dst - destination dynamic string (in out)
-- - src - source string (dynamic or fixed-capacity)
-- Returns:
-- - bit - result from _string_append
-- Notes: Outlined (not pragma inline) so ROM is one **`call`** per use; see.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
function string_append(string in out dst, string in src) return bit is
   return _string_append(dst, src)
end function

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Description: Append with maximum resulting length (delegates to builtin).
-- Parameters:
-- - dst     - destination dynamic string (in out)
-- - src     - source string
-- - max_len - maximum length after append (byte actuals are promoted)
-- Returns:
-- - bit - result from _string_append_truncate
-- Notes: Outlined — single ROM body; **`call`** at each use.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
function string_append_truncate(string in out dst, string in src,word in max_len) return bit is
   return _string_append_truncate(dst, src, max_len)
end function

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Description: Truncate dynamic string to max_len (delegates to builtin).
-- Parameters:
-- - dst     - destination dynamic string (in out)
-- - max_len - new maximum length
-- Returns:
-- - bit - result from _string_truncate
-- Notes: Outlined — single ROM body.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
function string_truncate(string in out dst, word in max_len) return bit is
   return _string_truncate(dst, max_len)
end function

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Description: Copy bytes from a byte array into a dynamic string (delegates to builtin).
-- Parameters:
-- - dst       - destination dynamic string (in out)
-- - src_array - source byte array (open array / fixed)
-- Returns:
-- - bit - result from _string_from_array
-- Notes: Outlined — single ROM body.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
function string_from_array(string in out dst, byte in src_array[]) return bit is
   return _string_from_array(dst, src_array)
end function

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Description: Copy from byte array into dynamic string with max length (delegates to builtin).
-- Parameters:
-- - dst       - destination dynamic string (in out)
-- - src_array - source byte array
-- - max_len   - maximum bytes to copy
-- Returns:
-- - bit - result from _string_from_array_truncate
-- Notes: Outlined; returns FALSE if truncated.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
function string_from_array_truncate(string in out dst, byte in src_array[], word in max_len) return bit is
   return _string_from_array_truncate(dst, src_array, max_len)
end function

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Description: Copy dynamic string into a byte array (delegates to builtin).
-- Parameters:
-- - dst_array - destination byte array (open array / fixed)
-- - src       - source string (dynamic or fixed-capacity)
-- Returns:
-- - bit - result from _string_to_array
-- Notes: Outlined — single ROM body.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
function string_to_array(byte out dst_array[], string in src) return bit is
   return _string_to_array(dst_array, src)
end function

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Description: Copy string into byte array with max bytes written (delegates to builtin).
-- Parameters:
-- - dst_array - destination byte array
-- - src       - source string
-- - max_len   - maximum bytes to write
-- Returns:
-- - bit - result from _string_to_array_truncate
-- Notes: Outlined; returns FALSE if truncated.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
function string_to_array_truncate(byte out dst_array[], string in src, word in max_len) return bit is
   return _string_to_array_truncate(dst_array, src, max_len)
end function

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Description: Pack string heap and relocate handles (delegates to builtin).
-- Parameters:
-- - (none)
-- Returns:
-- - bit - result from _string_heap_compact
-- Notes: Outlined — Phase B **`_string_heap_compact`** is large; **`call`** here avoids duplicating it at every call site (**`progress.md`** PIC18 ROM **B**).
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
function string_heap_compact() return bit is
   return _string_heap_compact()
end function



--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Float -> text renderer: lives in its own heap-free file so that callers
-- that only need float formatting (print_float_exact) do not pull the heap.
-- The function body is unchanged (moved 2026-10-21).
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
include float_str
